 "description": "HYP-01 (val4): exact ties of the log-ratio series inside bd0. In every row of P (BINOM.DIST) and Q (POISSON.DIST) the stored sum v + s of the series ln(x/M) = 2(v + sum v^(2k+1)/(2k+1)), v = (x-M)/(x+M), is an exact tie between two doubles, and the pmf differs by one or more ulp with the direction of that single rounding. P!D38:D41 are the three factors of HYPGEOM.DIST(12,17,15,21,FALSE) at p = 12/21 (computed in the sheet, and as a 15-digit literal). Sheet H is the val2 factor bridge (E, F against K = (H/J)*I) on 12 tuples one of whose factors holds such a tie; row 2 is the one cached tuple where the bridge is one ulp off the engine's model. Frozen predictions for both directions: docs/research/val4-hyp-predictions.json. Predictions are hypotheses, NOT expected values. Precision!B2:B4 must retain 0.9999999999999998, 1, 1.0000000000000002; C2:C4 must be -1,0,1.",
